+# WibWob-DOS — Agent Constitution
+
+**This file is the primary constitution for agents working on WibWob-DOS.**
+Read it completely before touching any code. Cross-reference the subsystem
+docs in `.agents/` for deep dives.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Project Identity
+
+WibWob-DOS is a **symbient operating system** — a TUI desktop shared between
+two AI personas (Wib and Wob) and a human co-habitant. It is NOT a C++
+project. There is no engine, no cmake, no IPC protocol.
+
+**Runtime stack:**
+- Language: TypeScript
+- Runtime: Bun (not Node — use `bun run`, not `node`)
+- TUI: blessed (terminal widget library)
+- API server: FastAPI (Python) — `src/api/`
+- Multiplayer: PartyKit — `src/services/party-*.ts`
+- Module system: dynamic microapps loaded at startup from `microapps/` and `microapps-private/`
+
+**Key directories:**
+```
+src/core/          — app controller, window manager, command catalog/registry, theme
+src/services/      — state, control API, workspace, content, agent session, file actions
+src/windows/       — window factory functions (one per window type)
+microapps/           — public microapp modules (each has microapp.json + index.ts)
+microapps-private/   — private modules (git submodule, never commit here without separate submodule commit)
+.agents/           — machine-readable specs: architecture.md, invariants.md, control-api.md
+.pi/skills/        — specialist skill files loaded on demand by the agent
+.planning/         — epics, features, stories, spikes, refactor docs
+scripts/           — shell utilities: handover.sh, restart.sh, minimap.sh
+scratch/           — runtime outputs (captures, workspaces, logs) — gitignored
+```
+
+**The app is designed for equal human/agent control.** Every surface accessible
+to a human must be equally reachable by an agent via the control API or
+command registry. If an agent can't reach something, that is a bug.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Build and Dev Commands
+
+```bash
+# Start the app
+bun run dev              # watch mode
+bun run start            # one-shot
+
+# Type checking — ALWAYS run before committing
+bun run typecheck        # tsc --noEmit; must pass clean
+
+# Planning
+bun run planning:status  # print epic status table
+bun run planning:sync    # sync EPIC_STATUS.md from frontmatter
+
+# Handover doc
+bun run handover         # generates tmp/session-handover-YYYY-MM-DD.md
+
+# Live app is in tmux session 'wibwob'
+# Health check:
+curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8099/health
+# State:
+curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8099/state | python3 -m json.tool
+# Run a command:
+curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8099/commands/run \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"id":"theme.set","args":{"name":"wibwob-dark"}}'
+```
+
+**Restart the live app (preserve tmux session):**
+```bash
+APP_PID=$(ps aux | grep "bun run src/app.ts" | grep -v grep | awk '{print $2}')
+kill $APP_PID && sleep 3
+tmux send-keys -t wibwob 'bun run start' Enter
+sleep 8 && curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8099/health
+```
+NEVER use `kill -9` as first resort — blessed needs SIGTERM for terminal cleanup.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Architecture Map
+
+Eight subsystems. Know which one owns each concern.
+
+### 3.1 Command System
+
+**Files:** `src/core/command-catalog.ts`, `src/core/command-registry.ts`
+
+`command-catalog.ts` is the **single source of truth** for all user-visible
+commands. It defines IDs, labels, groups, menu/palette placements, and API/
+agent visibility. Every command defined ONCE. The `AppMenuActions` interface
+declares every handler type.
+
+`command-registry.ts` is the execution adapter. It builds menus, palette,
+and the API list from the catalog. It holds `LEGACY_COMMAND_ALIASES` for
+backward-compat ID resolution. `registry.run(id, args)` is the canonical
+dispatch path — used by the API, agent tools, and keyboard shortcuts.
+
+**Gotchas agents get wrong:**
+- Adding a new command in catalog without wiring the `actionKey` handler in
+  `app-controller.ts:getAppMenuActions()` — TypeScript will catch this
+- Using a hardcoded ID string elsewhere instead of running via registry
+- Forgetting to set `api: true, agent: true` on commands that should be
+  agent-visible (default is false)
+- Command IDs changed in merge 4e2500b — use the LEGACY_COMMAND_ALIASES for
+  old IDs; add new aliases there rather than breaking callers
+
+### 3.2 Window Manager
+
+**Files:** `src/core/window-manager.ts`, `src/core/types.ts` (WindowRecord), `src/core/window-chrome.ts`
+
+`WindowManager` owns z-order, focus, drag, resize, tile, cascade, close, and
+maximize. Implements `WindowFacade` (11-method interface in `window-facade.ts`).
+
+`WindowRecord` is the runtime descriptor for every open window. Each window
+type creates a `WindowRecord` via `windowManager.createFrame()` or a custom
+blessed box, then calls `windowManager.registerWindow(record)`.
+
+`window-chrome.ts` is the ONLY place window size math (chrome offsets) lives.
+Never inline `+2`, `+3`, `+6` in window code.
+
+**Gotchas:**
+- Shadow was disabled (leaves stale cells). Do NOT re-enable blessed shadow.
+  The `syncShadow` and `shadow.show/hide` code was removed intentionally.
+- `savedBounds` on `WindowRecord` tracks maximize state — do not mutate directly
+- `describeState()` on every registered window is contractual — omitting it
+  prints a console warning; it is heading toward mandatory
+- `sendInput(id, input)` signature — no `sender` param in current HEAD
+- After `registerWindow()`, always call `record.focus()` to bring to front
+
+### 3.3 App Controller
+
+**File:** `src/core/app-controller.ts` (~2050 lines)
+
+The composition root. Creates the screen, desktop, menu bar, status line,
+overlays, window manager, command registry, control API, and workspace
+service. Owns all window-opening private methods.
+
+`getAppMenuActions()` (line ~1086) wires every catalog `actionKey` to a
+private method. If you add a command to the catalog, you MUST add the handler
+here too — TypeScript enforces this via `AppMenuActions` interface.
+
+**Decomposition in progress.** Do not add more code here. New window families
+belong in `src/windows/` as factory functions.
+
+**Gotchas:**
+- `applyTheme()` must be called after any `setThemeVariant()` call — it
+  propagates tokens to menu bar, desktop, status line, and all windows
+- `this.overlays.openListPrompt()` not `openCenteredListPrompt()` — the
+  centered variant does not exist in current HEAD
+- Workspace restore is async; `getLastWindow()` after `await openX()` may miss
+  the window — use `windowManager.getWindows()` after restore if needed
+
+### 3.4 Module System
+
+**Files:** `src/services/microapp-loader.ts`, each `microapps/*/microapp.json`
+
+Modules are directories with `microapp.json` and `index.ts`. They register
+window types, commands, themes, and snapshot handlers dynamically at startup.
+
+`microapp.json` declares `name`, `type` (`microapp` | `theme` | `primers`),
+`entry` (default `index.ts`), and type-specific config.
+
+The loader calls `setup(host: MicroappHost)` on `index.ts`'s default export.
+`host.registerCommand()` wires into the command registry. `host.registerSnapshot()`
+hooks workspace save/restore. `host.createWindow()` creates blessed windows.
+
+**Gotchas:**
+- `microapps-private/` is a git submodule — NEVER `git add microapps-private/` in
+  the parent repo. Changes need a separate commit inside the submodule.
+- Theme modules export a `ThemeVariant` as either default or named export
+- Microapp commands use LOCAL IDs (`"open"`) — the registry prefixes them with
+  the module namespace (e.g. `"microapp.wibwob.poetry-clock.open"`)
+- The ISO viewer serialises `{ seed, terrainIdx, seaLevel, levels }` — NOT
+  `sourcePath` (ephemeral file path). Do not regress this.
+
+### 3.5 State and Control API
+
+**Files:** `src/services/state-service.ts`, `src/services/control-api.ts`
+
+`StateService` owns canonical live desktop state. Every window reports
+semantic content via `describeState()`. The state is the source of truth for
+agent tools, workspace save, and API responses.
+
+`ControlAPI` exposes HTTP endpoints on port 8099 (default). See
+`.agents/control-api.md` for the full endpoint list.
+
+**Key endpoints agents use constantly:**
+```
+GET  /health               — wait for this before any other call
+GET  /state                — full window list with ids, positions, state
+GET  /commands/list        — all command ids with descriptions
+POST /commands/run         — {"id":"command-id","args":{}}
+POST /windows/input        — {"id":N,"input":"text\r"}  ← \r submits
+POST /view/primer/open     — {"filePath":"/abs/path","x":X,"y":Y,"w":W,"h":H}
+```
+
+**Gotchas:**
+- Always `GET /state` first to get real window IDs — never guess
+- `/commands/run` goes through the legacy alias map — old IDs work
+- `POST /windows/input` requires `\r` (not `\n`) to submit in interactive windows
+- The sessionId in `/health` is a 3-char slug — use it to verify you're talking
+  to the right instance when two are running
+
+### 3.6 Workspace and Snapshots
+
+**Files:** `src/services/workspace-service.ts`, `src/core/workspace-snapshots.ts`, `src/core/snapshot-registry.ts`
+
+Workspace = persisted JSON of open windows, positions, sizes, and per-window
+state. Saved to `scratch/workspaces/default.json` automatically.
+
+Each window type implements serialize + restore via `snapshot-registry.ts`.
+Microapps use `host.registerSnapshot({ serialize, restore })`.
+
+**Rules:**
+- Serialize PARAMS not ephemeral paths (`seed/terrainIdx` not `sourcePath`)
+- `describeState()` must set `appType` or the serialize guard will bail
+- Restore must degrade gracefully if payload is missing or partial
+
+### 3.7 Theme System
+
+**Files:** `src/core/theme/resolver.ts`, `src/core/theme/types.ts`, `src/core/theme/{dark,light,dark-pastel,dark-nord}.ts`, `microapps-private/wibwob-theme-*/theme.ts`
+
+`ThemeTokens` defines the full semantic token set (23 tokens). Every window
+uses `theme().body`, `theme().header`, etc. — never raw blessed colour strings.
+
+`toggleTheme()` cycles variants. `setThemeVariant(v)` sets a specific one.
+`allVariants()` returns all registered variants. `registerExternalTheme(v)`
+adds module-provided themes.
+
+**After any theme change:** call `applyTheme()` in app-controller to propagate
+tokens to shell chrome and all windows via `windowManager.restyleAll()`.
+
+**Gotchas:**
+- `safeSetStyle()` in `ui-primitives.ts` handles blessed's awkward scrollbar
+  sub-style fields — use it instead of direct `.style =` on widgets with items
+- External theme modules: loader accepts either `default` or named export that
+  has `.name` and `.tokens`
+
+### 3.8 Agent Session
+
+**Files:** `src/services/wibwob-agent-session.ts`, `src/windows/wibwob-agent-window.ts`, `src/services/agent-tools.ts`
+
+`WibWobAgentSession` owns model selection, tool wiring, and desktop state
+injection via `transformContext`. All file operations are jailed to REPO_ROOT.
+
+`agent-tools.ts` exposes TUI tools: `tui_get_state`, `tui_list_commands`,
+`tui_menu_command`, `tui_batch_layout`, `tui_screenshot`, etc. These wrap the
+`TuiToolContext` which wraps `WindowFacade`.
+
+**Lifecycle (multi-turn):**
+- `message_start` → no-op (entry created lazily)
+- `message_update` (text_delta) → creates entry on first delta if none exists
+- `message_end` → finalises text, clears `currentAssistantId`
+- `agent_end` → clears `currentAssistantId`, status = Ready
+Do NOT pre-create assistant entries in `send()` or create them in
+`message_start` — this was the transcript leak bug fixed in commit b0826fa.
+
