+## 5. Commit Conventions
+
+```
+<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary, lowercase, ≤72 chars>
+```
+
+**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `ci`, `spike`
+
+**Scopes:** `app`, `tui`, `window`, `microapp`, `module`, `theme`, `api`,
+`llm`, `agent`, `primer`, `workspace`, `command`, `snapshot`, `build`, `planning`
+
+**One logical change = one commit.** Typecheck must pass before every commit.
+
+Examples:
+```
+feat(command): add theme.choose interactive picker
+fix(workspace): serialize terrain params not ephemeral sourcePath
+fix(agent): clear assistant entry between turns, prevent transcript leak
+docs(planning): mark E022 S03 done
+chore(planning): close TODO-f9c4afb7 command regression
+```
+
+Multi-line body encouraged for non-trivial changes. Explain WHY, not WHAT.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Planning Conventions
+
+**Epics** live in `.planning/epics/eNNN-*/eNNN-brief.md` with YAML frontmatter:
+```yaml
+---
+id: E022
+title: WibWobWorld Restore & Layout Fidelity
+status: in-progress   # not-started | in-progress | blocked | done | dropped
+issue: 116
+pr: ~
+depends_on: [E018]
+---
+```
+
+**Stories** use body-level status: `Status: in-progress`
+
+**Checkboxes:** `[ ]` not started, `[~]` in progress, `[x]` done, `[-]` dropped
+
+**After landing a story:**
+1. Tick tasks `[x]` in story brief, set `Status: done`, add `PR: #NNN`
+2. Tick story in parent feature checklist
+3. If all features done: set epic `status: done`, run `bun run planning:sync`
+
+**GitHub issues exist at epic level only.** Stories/features/tasks live in
+`.planning/` briefs. Do not create GitHub issues for stories.
+
+---
+
+## 7. What NOT to Do
+
+These are failure modes agents have hit repeatedly.
+
+### Code
+
+- **DO NOT** use `kill -9` on the app process as a first resort. SIGTERM
+  (`kill $PID`) lets blessed clean up the terminal. Use `kill -9` only as
+  a last resort and run `reset` afterward.
+
+- **DO NOT** add inline size math (`+2`, `+3`, `+6`) in window code.
+  Chrome sizes belong in `window-chrome.ts`. Content sizes belong in
+  `content-measurement.ts`.
+
+- **DO NOT** re-enable blessed shadow. `shadow: true` leaves stale cells on
+  move/resize/close. The `syncShadow()` code was removed intentionally.
+
+- **DO NOT** add `sourcePath` back as an ISO viewer restore key. The file is
+  ephemeral (gitignored). Serialize `{ seed, terrainIdx, seaLevel, levels }`.
+  This regression was fixed in commit 5b1e255.
+
+- **DO NOT** commit changes to `microapps-private/` via the parent repo.
+  The submodule has its own git history. Stage and commit inside
+  `microapps-private/` first, then update the parent's submodule pointer.
+
+- **DO NOT** add a second measurement path for a caller that already has one.
+  One measurement function per content type. If you need measurement
+  somewhere new, call the existing `content-measurement.ts` functions.
+
+- **DO NOT** skip `describeState()` on new window types. It is heading toward
+  mandatory. Omitting it silently breaks workspace restore and agent state.
+
+- **DO NOT** add one-off text prompts when `OverlayManager.openListPrompt()`
+  can do the job. Shared pickers are the pattern.
+
+- **DO NOT** extend `restoreSafeMode` (the old workspace safe-mode flag).
+  It was removed. The correct approach is per-window graceful degradation
+  in the `restore` handler.
+
+- **DO NOT** set `currentAssistantId` in `send()` or create assistant entries
+  eagerly in `message_start`. Lazy creation in `message_update` is correct.
+  Pre-creating entries causes multi-turn transcript leaks.
+
+### Planning
+
+- **DO NOT** mark ACs done based on follow-on progress. ACs are binary.
+
+- **DO NOT** create GitHub issues for stories or features. Only epics get issues.
+
+- **DO NOT** edit `EPIC_STATUS.md` directly. It is generated by
+  `bun run planning:sync` from epic frontmatter.
+
+- **DO NOT** add planning content to `workings/` and expect it to be normative.
+  `workings/` is informational only. `.planning/` is the source of truth.
+
+### Agents
+
+- **DO NOT** guess window IDs. Always `GET /state` first.
+
+- **DO NOT** send bare text to agent windows without `\r` to submit.
+
+- **DO NOT** assume the live app is running. Check `/health` first.
+
+- **DO NOT** spawn a second app instance on port 8099. Use
+  `CONTROL_API_PORT=8098 SCRATCH_DIR=scratch/alt` for the alt instance.
+
