+## 9. Frequently Confused Things
+
+### "My command exists but run() returns Unknown command"
+
+1. Check `api: true, agent: true` in the catalog definition
+2. Check `LEGACY_COMMAND_ALIASES` — you may need to add an alias for the old ID
+3. Dynamic commands (from modules) are registered after startup — call
+   `GET /commands/list` to see current live set, not the static catalog
+
+### "Window opened but not visible / blank"
+
+1. Is the window registered with `windowManager.registerWindow(record)`?
+2. Did `frame.focus()` get called?
+3. Did `screen.render()` get called after content was set?
+4. Check `frame.body` dimensions — if width/height are 0, layout hasn't run
+
+### "Workspace restore opens wrong window or crashes"
+
+1. `describeState()` must set `appType` — the serialize guard checks it
+2. Snapshot `serialize` returning `undefined` disables restore silently
+3. Restore must not throw — wrap in try/catch and degrade to `runCommand("open")`
+
+### "Theme change doesn't update all windows"
+
+Call `this.applyTheme()` in app-controller after `setThemeVariant()`. It calls
+`windowManager.restyleAll()` which triggers every window's `onRestyle()`.
+If you set the variant directly without going through `applyTheme()`, the
+shell chrome (menu bar, desktop, status line) stays on the old theme.
+
+### "Module changes not picked up after restart"
+
+Module loader scans at startup only. Restart the app after changing
+`microapp.json` or `index.ts` in a module directory. For `microapps-private/`,
+also check the submodule pointer is updated in the parent repo.
+
+### "TypeScript errors after adding a new actionKey"
+
+`AppMenuActions` in `command-catalog.ts` is an interface. Adding a new
+`actionKey` to a command definition requires:
+1. Adding the method to `AppMenuActions`
+2. Implementing it in `app-controller.ts:getAppMenuActions()`
+
+TypeScript will error on both if you miss either step — this is intentional.
+
